# Patterns are matched against paths relative to the build context root, which
# is the repo root (see docker/docker-compose.yml). A bare `.env` therefore
# only excludes `<root>/.env` and would let `docker/.env` — where the README
# tells you to put real secrets — get baked into the image. Match at any depth.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
docs/
playwright/
scripts/
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/.cache
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE
.changeset/
.vscode/
